.git
.env
.env.*
.npmrc
.secrets
**/.secrets
.ops-backups
**/.ops-backups
private-backups
**/private-backups
automation-logs
**/automation-logs
deploy/phala/*.env
node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
**/.next
dist
**/dist
bin
**/bin
obj
**/obj
coverage
**/coverage
playwright-report
test-results
.morpheus-relayer-state*.json

# Rust build output: a local `target/` would be copied into the context only for
# the builder stage to rebuild it anyway, and it is hundreds of megabytes.
target
**/target
# `bin` and `**/bin` above are Node conventions, and one of them happens to match
# the signer service's process entry point (`workers/neo-signer/src/bin`). These
# two lines re-include that path and only that path; a cargo build in the image
# fails loudly without it, rather than shipping a service with no listener.
!workers/neo-signer/src/bin
!workers/neo-signer/src/bin/**
# `crates/nitro-attest/src/bin` is hit by the same `**/bin` rule (its
# `nsm-attest-rs` binary lives there); re-include it for the same reason.
!crates/nitro-attest/src/bin
!crates/nitro-attest/src/bin/**
